        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As per <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3496008044\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28130\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28130/hovercard?comment_id=3421572401&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28130#issuecomment-3421572401\">#28130 (comment)</a>, I managed to get the data on windowAudio option default values wrong. This PR aims to correct the data.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28246",
            "title": "Correct windowAudio option default values for Chrome and Edge",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-20T10:59:47.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-20T10:58:40.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In Chrome 140+, there are multiple places in WebGPU methods where a <code class=\"notranslate\">GPUTextureView</code> was expected, but now you can specify a <code class=\"notranslate\">GPUTexture</code> as a shorthand, provided a default <code class=\"notranslate\">GPUTextureView</code> is desired (it is equivalent to a <code class=\"notranslate\">GPUTextureView</code> created using a call to <code class=\"notranslate\">GPUTexture.createView()</code> with no descriptor specified).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-140#shorthand_for_using_texture_where_texture_view_is_used\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-140#shorthand_for_using_texture_where_texture_view_is_used</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds data points in the appropriate places.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28245",
            "title": "Chrome 140 Specify GPUTexture in place of GPUTextureView for default views",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-20T09:37:59.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-20T09:27:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF145 makes <code class=\"notranslate\">RTCEncodedAudioFrame</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">RTCEncodeVideoFrame</code> get constructors in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1975032\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1975032</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">These include an <code class=\"notranslate\">options.metadata</code> property that contains the same kind of object as returned by <code class=\"notranslate\">getMetadata()</code>.<br>\nThis adds the subfeatures for both cases which duplicate each other.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The results are based on test <a href=\"https://jsfiddle.net/jib1/5t1mehn4/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://jsfiddle.net/jib1/5t1mehn4/</a> from <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1975032#c7\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1975032#c7</a> along with version support for the whole thing went into Safari (26 - <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/17333/webkit-features-in-safari-26-0/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/blog/17333/webkit-features-in-safari-26-0/</a>).<br>\nThe test worked for Chrome, but not in browserstack. Therefore I have assumed that except for audioLevel the properties were added in first release of the constructor.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that the last commit adds sequenceNumber and recieveTime. I cannot see these in the test above, but was able to observed them in WPT tests by debugging. <a class=\"commit-link\" data-hovercard-type=\"commit\" data-hovercard-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/commit/68f2acd5e373c411df4cfea2cad744e655d39f67/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/commit/68f2acd5e373c411df4cfea2cad744e655d39f67\"><tt>68f2acd</tt></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3510275107\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41508\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41508/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41508\">mdn/content#41508</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28242",
            "title": "Ff145 RTCEncodedAudioFrame/RTCEncodeVideoFrame constructor/metadata",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-20T04:52:49.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-20T03:42:12.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
