        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fixes the Safari support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">CredentialsContainer</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">prf</code> extension, assuming it was accidentally marked as partial.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Safari is only available on macOS.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Originally introduced in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3323690981\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27586\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27586/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27586\">#27586</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28227",
            "title": "Unmark `CredentialsContainer` `prf` extension as partial in Safari",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-17T17:08:17.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-17T17:07:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updates our mirroring logic to ignore <code class=\"notranslate\">partial_implementation</code></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>when mirroring from desktop to mobile, and</li>\n<li>the <code class=\"notranslate\">notes</code> clearly refer to OS limitations.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fixes inconsistent mirroring data (esp. WebGPU in Chrome Android) until we aligned on <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3252114150\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27364\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27364/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27364\">#27364</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Disclaimer: Co-authored with Claude Code.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Triggered by <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3525941023\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28224\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28224/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28224\">#28224</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Partially caused by <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3513385654\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28184\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28184/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28184\">#28184</a>, in which I marked all WebGPU as partial in Chrome, without checking the impact on Chrome Android.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28226",
            "title": "feat(mirror): ignore OS limitations when mirroring to mobile",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-17T17:07:58.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-17T16:25:55.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF145 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">Idempotency-Key</code> header in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1991641\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1991641</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This has a spec <a href=\"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-httpapi-idempotency-key-header/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-httpapi-idempotency-key-header/</a> but adding it results in an error. Can you remind me how to get an exception?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The key is sent in requests to indicate that a POST/PATCH is a particular unique command. If the server gets the same request with the same key it ignores it.<br>\nAs specified the server defines the requirements for the key, which would be expected therefore to be unknown to the browser, and set by Javascript.<br>\nAs such you wouldn't expect a browser integration, and hence no BCD entry.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">However FF automatically attaches a key if one is not attached. As discussed in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1991641#c6\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1991641#c6</a> this is probably because the server doesn't really need to care what the key does. This then is the reason to indicate integration.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3510231336\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41497\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41497/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41497\">mdn/content#41497</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28219",
            "title": "FF145 Idempotency-Key HTTP header",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-17T02:45:22.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-17T02:44:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds details about the support of masque proxy in the <code class=\"notranslate\">proxy</code> API in support of <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1988988\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1988988</a> Add extension API support for masque proxy.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related content changes in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3522562741\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41563\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41563/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41563\">mdn/content#41563</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28213",
            "title": "Bug 1988988 support for masque in `proxy` API",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-16T17:18:11.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-16T16:38:24.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 138 adds the ability for a <code class=\"notranslate\">GPUBuffer</code> to be passed directly into a <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/GPUDevice/createBindGroup\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">GPUDevice.createBindGroup()</code></a> call as a binding resource in place of a <code class=\"notranslate\">GPUBufferBinding</code> object, provided the default <code class=\"notranslate\">size</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">offset</code> values are being used.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-138#shorthand_for_using_buffer_as_a_binding_resource\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-138#shorthand_for_using_buffer_as_a_binding_resource</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a data point for the new feature.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28212",
            "title": "Chrome 138 pass GPUBuffer directly as binding resource",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-20T12:52:15.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-16T14:40:14.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In Chrome 138, the size requirements for <code class=\"notranslate\">GPUBuffer</code>s mapped at creation have changed. During a <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/GPUDevice/createBuffer\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">GPUDevice.createBuffer()</code></a> call, if <code class=\"notranslate\">mappedAtCreation</code> is set <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">size</code> is not a multiple of <code class=\"notranslate\">4</code>, a <code class=\"notranslate\">RangeError</code> exception is thrown.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-138#size_requirement_changes_for_buffers_mapped_at_creation\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-138#size_requirement_changes_for_buffers_mapped_at_creation</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a data point for the change.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28210",
            "title": "Chromium 138 size requirement changes for GPUBuffers mapped at creation",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-20T12:48:29.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-16T13:46:59.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        }
    ]
